{
  "id": "kin-selection",
  "term": "kin selection",
  "definition": "Kin selection is a way cooperation can evolve when interactions are not random and individuals are more likely than chance to interact with others like themselves, such as relatives. In this sense, greater relatedness can help cooperative behavior spread in a population.",
